ient to be online at the same time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="725782">email</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1597642">imeyiri</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10041_725782_504392"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of exchanging messages and computer files over a network that does not require the sender and recipient to be online at the same time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="725782">email</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504392">imeyili</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10041_725782_505829"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A method of exchanging messages and computer files over a network that does not require the sender and recipient to be online at the same time.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="725782">email</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="505829">ubutumwa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10048_1167260_1805510"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An object (such as a customer, item, or employee) that shares a set of defined attributes or characteristics, and that is used to manage rules for data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1167260">external content type</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1805510">Ubwoko bw'ibiri inyuma</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10048_51300_1805510"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An object (such as a customer, item, or employee) that shares a set of defined attributes or characteristics, and that is used to manage rules for data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="51300">entity</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1805510">Ubwoko bw'ibiri inyuma</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10052_58226_504442"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A quick movement of a finger or pen on a screen that the computer interprets as a command, rather than as a mouse movement, writing, or drawing.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="58226">gesture</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504442">ikimenyetso</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1006_318140_505723"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">One of four fields of an SCODE. It is a unique number that is assigned to represent the error or warning.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318140">error code</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="505723">kodi y'ikosa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10069_338533_505877"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">In printing, the process of eliminating white lines between colors by printing small areas of overlapping color where colors touch.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="338533">trapping</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="505877">gusubiranya</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10077_33192_504240"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The ) character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="33192">closing parenthesis</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504240">ugakubo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10086_263114_1805536"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Pertaining to a file format that does not allow for VBA code. Office 12 default file formats are macro-free. Examples of file extensions for macro-free formats are .docx, .pptx, .xlsx.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="263114">macro-free</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1805536">makoro ziboneka</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="10089_227651_1576486"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">As one aspect of a KPI, the desired level of performance with respect to a specific business goal or strategy. Actual values are evaluated against the target to determine KPI score and status.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="227651">target</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1576486">gusimbuza igishya</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">