ing program designed to accomplish a specific result, such as introducing a new product or increasing market share.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="27187">campaign</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504188">kwamamaza</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12068_335551_504188"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A marketing program designed to accomplish a specific result, such as introducing a new product or increasing market share.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="335551">marketing campaign</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504188">kwamamaza</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="12069_150202_505044"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The pairing of two or more actions that are performed together as a single action; the action succeeds or fails as a whole.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="150202">transaction</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="505044">ikomatanya</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="gram