ursor down to the top of the next page or a specific number of lines. Its function may vary in different programs.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="89979">PAGE DOWN key</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504662">buto PAGE DOWN</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="14106_234578_1910119"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A room, computer, or any equipment needed at a meeting.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="234578">resource</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1910119">igikoresho</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1411_134356_504903"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A group of computers that are connected on a network and share resources, such as printers and files.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="134356">workgroup</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504903">itsinda ry'abakozi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected