d color that helps you keep track of items, such as messages, contacts, and appointments. You can use color categories to easily find, sort, filter, or group items.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650174">color category</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1910222">icyiciro cy'ibara</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1782_130364_2630424"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The representation of information and data in the form of an image, diagram, or animation. For example, some databases can interpret and show data in the form of a two- or three-dimensional model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="130364">visualization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2630424">kureba amakurushingiro</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1782_2396693_2630424"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The representation of information and data in the form of an image, diagram, or animation. For example, some databases can interpret and show data in the form of a two- or three-dimensional model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2396693">visual</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2630424">kureba amakurushingiro</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="1782_2626823_2630424"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The representation of information and data in the form of an image, diagram, or animation. For example, some databases can interpret and show data in the form of a two- or three-dimensional model.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2626823">data visualization</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2630424">kureba amakurushingiro</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17823_650183_1910223"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A format, such as cell shading or font color, that Excel automatically applies to cells if a specified condition is true.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650183">conditional format</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1910223">imiterere kigombero</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17827_650187_1910224"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A view of an individual contact that contains all the information stored in the contact.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650187">contact form</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1910224">ifishi y'uwo mutumanaho</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17828_650188_1910225"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of buttons used to move through contact items displayed in Address Cards or Detailed Address Cards view. The Contact index moves the focus to the first contact whose name begins with the selected character.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650188">Contact index</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1910225">Urutondeshakiro rw'abo mutumanaho</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="17831_650191_1805495"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The shape of how scheduled work for an assignment is distributed across time. Use a contour to control how Project schedules the work of a resource.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="650191">contour</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><