e signature as their counterparts that use the bubbling event routing strategy.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="206426">tunneling</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="505171">tanoringi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="28204_1475084_1910555"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The upper limit in a permitted range of values.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="1475084">upper bound</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1910555">ingano yo hejuru</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="2824_2685641_504488"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A listing of keywords and associated data that point to the location of more comprehensive information, such as files and records on a disk or record keys in a database.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="2685641">search index</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504488">umugerekashakiro</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type=