 as a message or file through a communications channel.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="110059">send</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504759">kohereza</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6175_766467_1597641"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To transmit content such as a message or file through a communications channel.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="766467">email</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1597641">kohereza imeyiri</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6175_766467_504759"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To transmit content such as a message or file through a communications channel.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="766467">email</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504759">kohereza</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6177_264614_505471"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The process of merging information into a document from a data source, such as an address book or database, to create customized documents, such as form letters or mailing labels.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="264614">mail merge</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Mass</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="505471">guhuza ubutumwa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6184_107441_504743"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To enlarge or reduce the display of an item, such as a drawing or a proportional character font, by adjusting its size proportionally.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="107441">scale</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504743">kuringanyiza</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6186_418609_2062396"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A voice session that can be conducted between two or more telephones, two or more devices (such as computers or smartphones), or between two or more such devices and telephones.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="418609">call</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="2062396">guhamagara</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6190_142020_1909946"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">The small black square in the lower-right corner of a selected cell that can be used to copy data and to fill adjacent cells with a series of data.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="142020">fill handle</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1909946">akazu kuzuzwamo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6196_144404_1909967"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of information service used to configure messaging programs to send and receive email.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="144404">mail delivery service</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1909967">serivisi itanga ubutumwa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6197_76338_504563"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A file that stores messages generated by an application, service, or operating system that are used to track the operations performed.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="76338">log file</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504563">dosiye mbika</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="62_3160_504023"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A server located on a network between client software, such as a Web browser, and another server. It intercepts all requests to the server to determine whether it can fulfill them itself. If not, it forwards the request to another server.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="3160">proxy server</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504023">seriveri ya porogisi</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6200_50329_504395"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To insert information created in one program, such as a chart, an equation, an image, a video or a font, into another program or Web page.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="50329">embed</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504395">kongeramo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6202_70557_504514"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To reverse something or change it to its opposite.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="70557">invert</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504514">gucurika</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6208_147957_1988667"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A field that can show formatting and graphics, such as an embedded object, and not just text.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="147957">rich text field</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1988667">umwanya w'umwandiko utsindagiye</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="621_121364_504829"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of object within a process that runs program instructions. Using multiple threads allows concurrent operations within a process and enables one process to run different parts of its program on different processors simultaneously. A thread has its own set of registers, its own kernel stack, a thread environment block, and a user stack in the address space of its process.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="121364">thread</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504829">mugenaporogaramu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6224_144653_504996"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A placeholder for text or pictures that you insert into your document.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="144653">merge field</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504996">umwanya w'ikomatanyirizo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6231_144677_1909968"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A single cell that is created by combining two or more selected cells. The cell reference for a merged cell is the upper-left cell in the original selected range.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="144677">merged cell</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1909968">akazu kahujwe</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6232_141181_504972"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">An area upon which users can draw multiple shapes, such that the shapes can be moved and resized as a unit.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="141181">drawing canvas</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504972">ubuso bw'igishushanyo</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6239_264786_505478"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A view for delivering a presentation that provides the presenter with additional options for viewing and controlling its delivery.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="264786">Presenter View</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="505478">Uburyo bw'iyerekana</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">ProperNoun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6240_30724_504225"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A type of payment card where the supplier is paid by the card issuer. The card holder then pays the card issuer.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="30724">credit card</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504225">ikarita yo kwishyurwa</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6247_318716_505757"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A collection of compositions or memorabilia of a specific type or for a particular purpose, such as audio recordings, photographs, or documents.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="318716">album</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="505757">arubumu</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6250_105621_504738"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A return to a previous stable condition, as when the contents of a hard disk are restored from a backup after a destructive hard disk error.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="105621">rollback</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504738">isubiranya</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="626_61316_504459"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">Not visible to the user.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="61316">hidden</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504459">cyahishwe</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Adjective</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6273_145441_1909981"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">A set of software that provides access to a particular type of OLAP database. This software can include a data source driver and other client software that is necessary to connect to a database.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="145441">OLAP provider</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">Singular</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="1909981">Mutanga OLAP</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">NotSelected</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet></termEntry><termEntry id="6279_26739_504186"><langSet xml:lang="en-US"><descripGrp><descrip type="definition">To attempt to establish a voice conversation with another person or other people from a phone, computer, or mobile device.</descrip></descripGrp><ntig><termGrp><term id="26739">call</term><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Verb</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalNumber">NotSelected</termNote></termGrp></ntig></langSet><langSet xml:lang="rw-RW"><ntig><termGrp><term id="504186">guhamagara</term><termNote type="geographicalUsage">RWA</termNote><termNote type="partOfSpeech">Noun</termNote><termNote type="grammaticalGender">No